    delphi:hasVerdict "resolvable-now" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.9"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Soft-bodied fossil occurrences and taphonomic associations are directly documented in public data. The absolute non-preservation statement is readily falsifiable and the broader bias can be quantified." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Compare preservation frequencies by tissue mineralization and depositional regime, and test for wholly soft-bodied fossils and skeletal remains in condensed or nondepositional settings. Verified soft-bodied fossils directly refute the absolute first clause, while taphonomic patterns test the bias." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Exceptional preservation creates strong site-selection effects.", "Absence of preservation is difficult to distinguish from absence of organisms." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch09-04--gpt--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch09-04--gpt--dataset-2> .
